## Task 4: CNN Model Architecture

The CNN model is built using **TensorFlow/Keras** (see `notebook.ipynb` for full Keras implementation):

```python
model = Sequential([
    # Block 1
    Conv2D(32, (3, 3), padding='same', input_shape=(64, 64, 3)),
    Activation('relu'),
    MaxPooling2D(pool_size=(2, 2)),

    # Block 2
    Conv2D(64, (3, 3), padding='same'),
    Activation('relu'),
    MaxPooling2D(pool_size=(2, 2)),

    # Block 3
    Conv2D(128, (3, 3), padding='same'),
    Activation('relu'),
    MaxPooling2D(pool_size=(2, 2)),

    # Classifier Head
    Flatten(),
    Dense(128, activation='relu'),
    Dropout(0.4),
    Dense(4, activation='softmax')   # 4 classes
])

model.compile(optimizer='adam',
              loss='sparse_categorical_crossentropy',
              metrics=['accuracy'])
```

**Layer Summary:**

| Layer | Type | Output Shape | Parameters |
|---|---|---|---|
| conv2d_1 | Conv2D (32 filters, 3×3) + ReLU | (64, 64, 32) | 896 |
| max_pooling_1 | MaxPooling2D (2×2) | (32, 32, 32) | 0 |
| conv2d_2 | Conv2D (64 filters, 3×3) + ReLU | (32, 32, 64) | 18,496 |
| max_pooling_2 | MaxPooling2D (2×2) | (16, 16, 64) | 0 |
| conv2d_3 | Conv2D (128 filters, 3×3) + ReLU | (16, 16, 128) | 73,856 |
| max_pooling_3 | MaxPooling2D (2×2) | (8, 8, 128) | 0 |
| flatten | Flatten | (8192,) | 0 |
| dense_1 | Dense + ReLU | (128,) | 1,048,704 |
| dropout | Dropout (40%) | (128,) | 0 |
| dense_2 (output) | Dense + Softmax | (4,) | 516 |

